IMPORT prelude

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- REGULATIVE RULES of Order 16, Order 17 and Order 18: the duties and permissions of a named party with a period and a consequence the text states (roc3, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- Each rule here has a twin in the decision-function modules that decides the same duty over the facts; the twin is the one
-- that is asserted, because a DEONTIC value cannot be compared with EQUALS on this binary.  These rules are run with #TRACE
-- and their results are read by eye (the result line is recorded in NOTES.md under "What the main binary does not accept").
-- Time here is a plain number of days from the start of the trace.  `WITHIN` counts forward from the start, so a period the
-- Rules count BACKWARD ("at least 28 days before the hearing", O 15 r 4(3) and r 16(6)) cannot be written in it; those are
-- decided by the decision functions and the input `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` (PLAN.md 5.1).
-- O 3 r 2(1) is not threaded.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 16 -- Discontinuance`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 16 r 2(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 16 r 2(1) the claimant`

DECLARE `o 16 r 2(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 16 r 2(1) serve a notice in Form 32`

-- src:1644 | 2. —(1) The claimant in an action begun by originating claim may, without the permission of the Court, discontinue the action, or withdraw any particular claim made by the claimant therein, as against all or any of the defendants at any time not later than 14 days after service of the defence on the claimant or, if there are 2 or more defendants, of the defence last served, by serving a notice in Form 32 to that effect on the defendant concerned. (2) A defendant may, without the permission of the Court — ( a )
@ref O 16 r 2(1) (src:1644)
`o 16 r 2(1) the claimant may serve a notice in Form 32 after service of the defence` MEANS
    PARTY `o 16 r 2(1) the claimant`
    MAY `o 16 r 2(1) serve a notice in Form 32`
    WITHIN 14

-- Day 0 is the day the defence is served on the claimant.  The claimant serves on day 14: the permission was used.
#TRACE `o 16 r 2(1) the claimant may serve a notice in Form 32 after service of the defence` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 16 r 2(1) the claimant` DOES `o 16 r 2(1) serve a notice in Form 32` AT 14
-- The claimant lets the 14 days pass: the permission lapses without breach (a MAY).
#TRACE `o 16 r 2(1) the claimant may serve a notice in Form 32 after service of the defence` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 17 -- Judgments and orders`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 17 r 3(5) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 17 r 3(5) the party required to draw up the order`
    `o 17 r 3(5) any other party affected by the order`

DECLARE `o 17 r 3(5) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 17 r 3(5) send a draft of the order to the solicitors of all other parties`
    `o 17 r 3(5) draw up the order`

-- src:1679 | (5) The party who is required by this Rule to draw up an order must send a draft of the order to the solicitors (if any) of all other parties within 14 days after the order is made and if that party fails to do so, any other party affected by the order may draw it up.
@ref O 17 r 3(5) (src:1679)
`o 17 r 3(5) the party must send a draft of the order to the solicitors of all other parties` MEANS
    PARTY `o 17 r 3(5) the party required to draw up the order`
    MUST `o 17 r 3(5) send a draft of the order to the solicitors of all other parties`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (
        PARTY `o 17 r 3(5) any other party affected by the order`
        MAY `o 17 r 3(5) draw up the order`
    )

-- Day 0 is the day the order is made.
#TRACE `o 17 r 3(5) the party must send a draft of the order to the solicitors of all other parties` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 17 r 3(5) the party required to draw up the order` DOES `o 17 r 3(5) send a draft of the order to the solicitors of all other parties` AT 14
-- Day 15: the party has failed to send the draft; the residual is the other party's permission to draw it up.
#TRACE `o 17 r 3(5) the party must send a draft of the order to the solicitors of all other parties` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

DECLARE `o 17 r 3(6) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 17 r 3(6) the solicitors of the other parties`

DECLARE `o 17 r 3(6) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 17 r 3(6) respond to the draft with their consent or their amended draft`

-- src:1680 | (6) The solicitors of the other parties must respond to the draft with their consent or their amended draft within 2 days, failing which they are deemed to consent to the draft.
@ref O 17 r 3(6) (src:1680)
`o 17 r 3(6) the solicitors must respond to the draft` MEANS
    PARTY `o 17 r 3(6) the solicitors of the other parties`
    MUST `o 17 r 3(6) respond to the draft with their consent or their amended draft`
    WITHIN 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 17 r 3(6) the solicitors of the other parties` BECAUSE "failing which they are deemed to consent to the draft"

-- The deeming itself is the decision function `o 17 r 3(6) the solicitors are deemed to consent to the draft`.
#TRACE `o 17 r 3(6) the solicitors must respond to the draft` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 17 r 3(6) the solicitors of the other parties` DOES `o 17 r 3(6) respond to the draft with their consent or their amended draft` AT 2
#TRACE `o 17 r 3(6) the solicitors must respond to the draft` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 3)

