§ `Order 18 -- Appeals`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 18 r 9(3) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 9(3) the absent party`

DECLARE `o 18 r 9(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 9(3) apply to restore the appeal for rehearing`

-- src:1776 | (3) The Court may restore the appeal for rehearing upon the application of the absent party who must file and serve any such application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal within 14 days after the dismissal or hearing of the appeal and must show good reason for that party’s absence.
@ref O 18 r 9(3) (src:1776)
`o 18 r 9(3) the absent party may apply to restore the appeal` MEANS
    PARTY `o 18 r 9(3) the absent party`
    MAY `o 18 r 9(3) apply to restore the appeal for rehearing`
    WITHIN 14

-- Day 0 is the day of the dismissal or hearing of the appeal.
#TRACE `o 18 r 9(3) the absent party may apply to restore the appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 18 r 9(3) the absent party` DOES `o 18 r 9(3) apply to restore the appeal for rehearing` AT 14
#TRACE `o 18 r 9(3) the absent party may apply to restore the appeal` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

DECLARE `o 18 r 15 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 15 the appellant`

DECLARE `o 18 r 15 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 15 file and serve a notice of appeal in Form 35`

-- src:1819 | 15. A party who intends to appeal to a District Judge against a decision of the Registrar of the State Courts must file and serve on all parties who have an interest in the appeal a notice of appeal in Form 35 within 14 days after the date of the Registrar’s decision.
@ref O 18 r 15 (src:1819)
`o 18 r 15 the appellant must file and serve the notice of appeal` MEANS
    PARTY `o 18 r 15 the appellant`
    MUST `o 18 r 15 file and serve a notice of appeal in Form 35`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 18 r 15 the appellant` BECAUSE "within 14 days after the date of the Registrar’s decision"

-- Day 0 is the date of the Registrar's decision.
#TRACE `o 18 r 15 the appellant must file and serve the notice of appeal` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 18 r 15 the appellant` DOES `o 18 r 15 file and serve a notice of appeal in Form 35` AT 14
#TRACE `o 18 r 15 the appellant must file and serve the notice of appeal` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

DECLARE `o 18 r 20(1) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 20(1) the appellant`

DECLARE `o 18 r 20(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 20(1) provide security for the respondent’s costs and file a certificate in Form 36`

-- src:1879 | 20. —(1) The appellant must provide security for the respondent’s costs of the appeal and file a certificate for security for costs in Form 36 at the time the appellant files the notice of appeal. (2) Where there is more than one appellant in the same appeal, all the appellants need to provide only one set of security for the appeal.
@ref O 18 r 20(1) (src:1879)
`o 18 r 20(1) the appellant must provide security and file the certificate` MEANS
    PARTY `o 18 r 20(1) the appellant`
    MUST `o 18 r 20(1) provide security for the respondent’s costs and file a certificate in Form 36`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 18 r 20(1) the appellant` BECAUSE "at the time the appellant files the notice of appeal"

-- Day 0 is the day the appellant files the notice of appeal.
#TRACE `o 18 r 20(1) the appellant must provide security and file the certificate` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 18 r 20(1) the appellant` DOES `o 18 r 20(1) provide security for the respondent’s costs and file a certificate in Form 36` AT 0
#TRACE `o 18 r 20(1) the appellant must provide security and file the certificate` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1)

DECLARE `o 18 r 21(12) party` IS ONE OF
