DECLARE `o 18 r 21(14)(a) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 21(14)(a) the appellant or any party to the appeal`

DECLARE `o 18 r 21(14)(a) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 21(14)(a) request in writing to the appellate Court for directions`

-- src:1929 | (14) Where an appeal is deemed withdrawn pursuant to paragraph (12) and if there are any outstanding issues as to costs or other matters that remain between the parties to the appeal — ( a )
-- src:1930 | the appellant or any party to the appeal may, within 14 days after the date that the appeal is deemed withdrawn, request in writing to the appellate Court for directions on those issues;
-- src:1931 | ( b )
-- src:1932 | no oral arguments are to be made in a request under sub‑paragraph ( a ) unless the appellate Court otherwise directs; and
-- src:1933 | ( c )
-- src:1934 | the Registrar may, upon receiving a request under sub‑paragraph ( a ), give directions on the making of written submissions for the request.
@ref O 18 r 21(14) (src:1929-1934)
`o 18 r 21(14)(a) the party may request directions on the outstanding issues` MEANS
    PARTY `o 18 r 21(14)(a) the appellant or any party to the appeal`
    MAY `o 18 r 21(14)(a) request in writing to the appellate Court for directions`
    WITHIN 14

-- Day 0 is the date the appeal is deemed withdrawn.
#TRACE `o 18 r 21(14)(a) the party may request directions on the outstanding issues` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 18 r 21(14)(a) the appellant or any party to the appeal` DOES `o 18 r 21(14)(a) request in writing to the appellate Court for directions` AT 14

DECLARE `o 18 r 21(15) party` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 21(15) the respondent`

DECLARE `o 18 r 21(15) act` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 21(15) make submissions at the hearing of the appeal`

-- src:1935 | (15) Where the respondent to the appeal fails to file and serve the written submissions for the appeal within the specified time, the respondent is not allowed to make submissions at the hearing of the appeal unless the appellate Court otherwise orders.
@ref O 18 r 21(15) (src:1935)
GIVEN `the respondent fails to file and serve the written submissions for the appeal within the specified time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellate Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 18 r 21(15) party` `o 18 r 21(15) act`
`o 18 r 21(15) the respondent shall not make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the respondent fails to file and serve the written submissions for the appeal within the specified time` AND (NOT `the appellate Court has otherwise ordered`)
    THEN PARTY `o 18 r 21(15) the respondent` SHANT `o 18 r 21(15) make submissions at the hearing of the appeal`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The respondent failed in time and there is no order: the respondent makes submissions at the hearing (day 5), a breach.
#TRACE `o 18 r 21(15) the respondent shall not make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 18 r 21(15) the respondent` DOES `o 18 r 21(15) make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` AT 5
-- The respondent filed in time: the rule does not bind, so the same act is not a breach.
#TRACE `o 18 r 21(15) the respondent shall not make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 18 r 21(15) the respondent` DOES `o 18 r 21(15) make submissions at the hearing of the appeal` AT 5
